{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44810-atlantean-pantheon-and-the-internet","id":44810,"title":"Atlantean Pantheon and the Internet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-08T04:28:20-08:00","id":44810,"title":"Atlantean Pantheon and the Internet","content":"So, I was reading the write-up of the Atlantean Pantheon in Scion: Demigod, and I started thinking about how to make them viable patron-deities for starting characters, when it hit me while reading Kuros's entry: it sounds a lot like he'd be a natural fit for the God of the Internet, what with his focus on the instantaneous transmission of information and how he personified the &quot;information wants to be free&quot; meme.<br /> <br /> Then, I started thinking about the others, and it occured to me that the Atlantean Pantheon would probably fit quite well as The Pantheon of The Internet, dwelling in a God-Realm that sits in the middle of the World Wide Web. How this might come to be depends on what exactly happened during the Fall of Atlantis, but most likely it'd involve (one of) them awakening from their slumber/being reborn/escaping their imprisonment, and Kuros noticing that his domain is a lot stronger than it was before, before discovering the Internet that mortals have created and begun using to share information with each other instantaneously across the world.<br /> <br /> Amnis: Goddess of the Internet Cables? (Dunno, it's the weakest association)<br /> Badarus: God of Internet Surfing/Science<br /> Demosia: Goddess of Government Surveillance (NSA, I'm looking at you)<br /> Heshon: Goddess of the Wild and Untamed Internet (Hello, /b/)<br /> Kuros: God of Hackers and the Information Superhighway<br /> Skaft: Functionally unchanged<br /> Versak: God of Forum Moderators and Internet Police<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T08:19:29-08:00","id":44921,"title":"","content":"An interesting idea. I don't have a lot of input right now. I may need some time to contemplate.<br /> <br /> In the meantime? You may consider another option.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where you might find it at this point, but on the old forum, someone had this GREAT supplement written up that basically detailed the entire secret history of the fall of Atlantis and it's Gods. The whole thing gives you a walkthrough of how your players could go on an epic adventure to rescue the Atlantean Gods and return them to the World.<br /> <br /> In that supplement, it stated that the few Atlantean Gods who were still free developed a series of Magic Spells that allowed them to find Scions in the World with a spark of Atlantean divinity still in their blood. Then there was a spell to allow them to perform a &quot;remote Visitation&quot; upon that Scion and activate him/her as a Scion of whichever Atlantean God to which they were distantly related.<br /> <br /> The whole idea was that the downfall of Atlantis was engineered by Okeanus, (a Titan Avatar of the Drowned Road) who used the situation as an excuse to conquer the Atlantean godrealm.. He basically consumed Badarus into himself (it is possible to free him), he took Amnis as his forced concubine (also salvageable, though she's badly traumatized from thousands of years of rape and torture), Skaft is held prisoner and forced to build weapons for Okeanus' eventual invasion of the World, Kuros was turned to stone (reversible), and Versak was imprisoned in the Atlantean Underworld at a fraction of his former powers. Only Demosia and Heshon were free and able to attempt to assemble this &quot;Atlanteand resistance.&quot;<br /> <br /> If anyone knows where that file can be found, I'd appreciate it. I thought it was really good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}